reims-vgpu: a linear memo read vouches for the rest of its command buffer (arm in exec).

The guest linear memo witness (reims-linear-memo-witness) lets a sampled bind
skip re-reading a guest-CPU texture's span when the hypervisor's dirty
bitmap and this device's write record both vouch for it. The hypervisor half
has an arming window: a token tracked since the last doorbell reads
generation 0 until the next doorbell harvests it, and a long submission rings
no doorbell while it runs. A texture first sampled inside one was re-read on
every draw. On a drag starting on a Home-screen icon:
125 draws in one second sampled a new 1216x2688 RGBA16F span (25 MiB); 118
re-read and compared it (memo_read 316 ms + memo_cmp 219 ms of a 727 ms
sampled resolve, 839 ms drain), one CmdExecIndirect2 took 801 ms
(sync_exec_lock_hold, 97 draws), lmw_arm_unarmed 114 and lmw_unarmed 112,
lin_memo_vouched 7. On the screen the page did not follow the finger and the
swipe began 0.3-1.2 s after the release.

Now `runtime::linear_memo_witness` has scopes: `execute_submission` opens one
around each command buffer's walk and closes it after; every event record
starts a new one (`break_scope`). A read that confirms the memo while the
token's generation is still 0 records the scope, `host_writes.epoch()` and
the memo generation (`lmw_arm_scope`), and a later bind in the same scope is
vouched (`lmw_scope_vouched`, counted under lin_memo_vouched as well) when
the memo generation, page list and span are unchanged, `host_writes` is
quiet for the pages since the confirming read, and nothing submitted can
still write them. Outside a scope, or in another one, the arming window
refuses as before (`lmw_unarmed`).

Why a scope is sound for the guest half: every read in it runs after the
submission's doorbell, so every guest store ordered before the handoff is in
the bytes read. Metal leaves a resource's contents undefined when the CPU
writes it while a command buffer uses it; the one ordered way to write it
mid-buffer is an event the buffer waits on, and an event ends the scope. The
device half is unchanged, and scoped vouches share the audit stride (one in
64 reads and compares; a difference fails lin_memo_witness_unsound and drops
the vouch). REIMS_VGPU_LINEAR_MEMO_SCOPE=off turns scopes off.

Tests: linear_memo_witness::tests a_read_in_a_scope_vouches_for_that_scope_only,
no_scope_no_vouch_in_the_arming_window, an_event_breaks_the_scope,
a_scope_keeps_the_device_half, a_scope_is_audited_and_a_failed_audit_drops_it.

